From f0000183673d80f39fbb1a3b7dc5630b52fea0f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BellSoft <info@bell-sw.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 23:08:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(vendorjdk): match standalone vendor JDK and NIK runtimes
 against their OSV ecosystems

Local (vendor-specific) change, applied after the upstream series.

Add the vendor JDK matcher for the VendorJdkPkg and VendorNikPkg package
types reported by syft's java-vendor-jdk-cataloger. It searches by the
package's product ecosystem (the module's JDK and NIK families,
"<family>:<major>" / "<family>:<nik major>-<java major>") through the
vendordb provider; no CPE matching is attempted, so a runtime is never
reported twice. An unavailable archive follows the provider's policy
(warning by default, fatal in strict mode).

Both types use the JVM version format. A vendor runtime owned by an OS
package (an apk-installed JDK on the vendor Linux) is dropped by the
package overlap rules whatever the version notation, so only the apk
package's advisories are reported for it.
